    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is a differentiable function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math> lies in the interval",
